  "id": "index-of-discrimination",
  "term": "index of discrimination",
  "definition": "In assessment, an index of discrimination is a psychometric measure of how well a test item separates people who know the content from those who do not. A low index means the item does not clearly distinguish between more knowledgeable and less knowledgeable test-takers.",
